Verdict: SUPPORTED
Rationale: The evidence collectively establishes that both the Battle of Saipan and the Battle of Manila were fought by American forces. The Battle of Saipan was an amphibious assault by the United States against Japan during World War II, and the Battle of Manila (1945) was fought by forces from both the United States and the Philippines against Imperial Japanese troops. No reliable evidence contradicts this claim.
